  "chain_B": "pluto-5d4d \u2014 lnb-a or lnb-b, both DRY",
  "why": "load_pairs orders a pair's radios by radio_id, and pluto-19f2 sorts before pluto-5d4d",
  "not_identified": "WATER IS CONFOUNDED WITH RADIO. Chain A is always pluto-19f2 (lnb-c or lnb-d, both WET) and chain B always pluto-5d4d (lnb-a or lnb-b, both DRY), because the join orders a pair's radios by radio_id. Any gap between dA and dB is therefore a radio-and-water difference at once, and this corpus holds no dry port on 19f2 and no wet port on 5d4d to break the tie."
 },
